WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.950
The demolitions started, the
redevelopment started, and in 1961,

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.950
my family was given a flat on Calea Griviței,
right opposite the Grivița Roșie works,

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.950
opposite the old railway canteen,
which is now the MedLife Hyperclinic.

4
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.450
Right there. I still have the flat;
it came to me from my parents.

5
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:41.348
Bit by bit, the area grew. People started
getting flats, and they worked at all

6
00:00:41.398 --> 00:00:44.450
sorts of factories.

7
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.450
People seemed to stick
together much more back then.

8
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.450
Everyone would come out and
work, clearing the paths,

9
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.711
especially in winter, when the snow came.

10
00:00:57.761 --> 00:01:01.450
Winters were different
back then, not like now.

11
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:10.573
In the '60s, winter started in November,
around the middle of the month, and the

12
00:01:10.623 --> 00:01:14.450
snow might not go until mid-March.

13
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:20.450
When we moved in, in 1961…
our block has six entrances.

14
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:27.450
Of everyone who moved in
there, nobody had a car.

15
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.450
Nobody, nobody.

16
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:36.450
And I'd say it was the
same in the other blocks.

17
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:45.040
On Calea Griviței there are seven prefab
blocks, from Piața Chibrit towards what's

18
00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.450
now the Burns Hospital,

19
00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:53.450
built in '60, '61.

20
00:01:53.500 --> 00:02:00.450
After the winter, when spring
came and the snow melted,

21
00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:15.450
the road was full of potholes, and the
stonemasons would come and mend it with cobbles.

22
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:21.450
Lots of times I'd go out in
front of my block and watch them.

23
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:28.950
If I've managed to share a few memories
of what I lived through, I'm glad.

